+`[toolset.ask_user_question]` is honored across **requirements.toml**, **managed config**, and your user **`config.toml`**. Precedence: requirements → env (`GROK_ASK_USER_QUESTION_TIMEOUT_ENABLED` / `GROK_ASK_USER_QUESTION_TIMEOUT_SECS` / `GROK_ASK_USER_QUESTION_TIMEOUT_ACTION`) → user config → managed → defaults. Set `timeout_enabled = false` in your user config to disable the automatic questionnaire timeout for yourself; `timeout_secs` must be a positive integer. `timeout_action` is `"decline"` (official: timeout = Shift+X dismiss) or `"recommended"` (single-select: first option whose label contains `(Recommended)`, else the first option; multi-select: every `(Recommended)` label joined with `, `, same as a user submit; if none are marked, first option only). The tool result says it timed out and auto-selected; it does not fake a user click, and the waiting card's empty `[ ]` boxes are not the tool result. You can also toggle `timeout_enabled` from `/settings` → **Ask-Question timeout** (under Agent & Approval); `timeout_action` is config/env only. Changes apply to newly started sessions.
 
